===Dancing Puppets===
{{Magic Info
|magicimage=[[File:Dancing_Puppet.png|left]]
|magicname=踊る人形の矢, ''Odoru Ningyō no Ya''
|magicjp=矢, Arrow • の, of • 踊る, Dancing • 人形, Puppet
|magictl=Sign of Dancing Puppets{{Ref|m|6|11}}
|magicdesc=Official Name, Unofficial Description
|magictype=}}
The '''Sign of Dancing Puppets''' likely allows for the conscious manipulation of a target object’s movement, which can differ visually. Tetia’s usage of the sign causes her cloak to move erratically with seemingly no direction,{{Ref|m|6|11-12}}{{Ref|m|4}} while Sasaran’s usage allows him to move his cloak with incredible accuracy and precision.{{Ref|m|27|22}}

When '''Dancing Puppets''' is used alongside a sigil, the sigil can be placed in its center. When '''Dancing Puppets''' is paired with a '''Sigil of Wind''', it allows the target object to fly and be manipulated within the air. This sign may be semi-directional and has never been seen inverted. 

The '''Dancing Puppets’''' ability appears similar to that of the '''Sign of Sights Set''', with the key difference seeming to be that '''Sights Set''' requires the caster to actively aim the spell or object in some way. Meanwhile, spells using '''Dancing Puppets''' are able to be manipulated at long distances.{{Ref|m|6|11-12}}{{Ref|m|4}}{{Ref|m|27|22}}

Interestingly, there are spells with symbols that closely resemble that of '''Dancing Puppets''', namely [[Sealchair Spell]], [[Beldaruit's Illusion Cloak Spell]], [[Truth Spell]] and spells used by Engendale during his fight with Qifrey.{{Ref|m|68|12-13}} It is reasonable to assume this sign and '''Dancing Puppets''' are related.

