==Decorative Signs==
'''Decorative Signs''' are first introduced in [[Chapter 58]] as signs that give spells the rough shape of the creatures they're named after.{{Ref|m|58|22}} They are also referred to as '''Sculpting Signs''' (specifically Watersculpting Signs) in [[Chapter 62]].{{Ref|m|62|10}} From [[Chapter 78]] onwards, they are consistently referred to as [[Sigils|sigils]].{{Ref|m|78|17-19}} See [[Sigils Explained#Decorative Sigils|Decorative Sigils]] for a more in-depth description and a list of examples.
{{-}}'''Spells Using Decorative Signs'''<br>
[[Bird of Light Beacon]] • [[Fish Guidance]] • [[Flowers of Light]] • [[Glowing Owlcat]] • [[Valance Leech Counterclock]] • [[Valance Leech of Light]] • [[Watersculpture]] ([[Qifrey's Water Dragon|Water Dragon]] • [[Water Horse]] • [[Water Rose]])

